{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "EZK",
  "chapter": 41,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Afterward he brought me to the temple, and measured the posts, six cubits broad on the one side, and six cubits broad on the other side, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "which was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the breadth of the tabernacle.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the breadth of the door ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " ten cubits; and the sides of the door ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " five cubits on the one side, and five cubits on the other side: and he measured the length of it forty cubits: and the breadth, twenty cubits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then he went inward, and measured the post of the door, two cubits; and the door, six cubits; and the breadth of the door, seven cubits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So he measured the length of it twenty cubits; and the breadth, twenty cubits, before the temple: and he said to me, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the most holy ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "place",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Afterward he measured the wall of the house, six cubits; and the breadth of ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " side-chamber, four cubits, round the house on every side.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the side-chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three, one over another, and thirty in order; and they entered into the wall which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the house for the side-chambers around, that they might have hold, but they had not hold in the wall of the house.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an enlarging, and a winding about still upward to the side-chambers: for the winding about of the house went still upward around the house; therefore the breadth of the house ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was still",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " upward, and so increased ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "from",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the lowest ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "chamber",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the highest by the midst.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I saw also the hight of the house around: the foundations of the side-chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a full reed of six great cubits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The thickness of the wall, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the side-chamber without, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " five cubits: and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " left ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the place of the side-chambers that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " within.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And between the chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the width of twenty cubits around the house on every side.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the doors of the side-chambers ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towards ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the place that was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " left, one door towards the north, and another door towards the south: and the breadth of the place that was left ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " five cubits around.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now the building that was before the separate place at the end towards the west ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " seventy cubits broad; and the wall of the building ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " five cubits thick around, and its length ninety cubits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So he measured the house, a hundred cubits long; and the separate place, and the building, with its walls, a hundred cubits long;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Also the breadth of the face of the house, and of the separate place towards the east, a hundred cubits.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he measured the length of the building over against the separate place which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " behind it, and its galleries on the one side and on the other side, a hundred cubits, with the inner temple, and the porches of the court;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The door posts, and the narrow windows, and the galleries around on their three stories, over against the door, ceiled with wood around, and from the ground up to the windows, and the windows ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " covered;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To that above the door, even to the inner house, and without, and by all the wall around within and without, by measure.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " made with cherubim and palm-trees, so that a palm-tree ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " between a cherub and a cherub; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "every",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cherub had two faces;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So that the face of a man ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " towards the palm-tree on the one side, and the face of a young lion towards the palm-tree on the other side: ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " made through all the house around.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "From the ground to above the door ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " cherubim and palm-trees made, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "on",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the wall of the temple.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The posts of the temple ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " squared, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the face of the sanctuary; the appearance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the one",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " as the appearance ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of the other",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The altar of wood ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " three cubits high, and its length two cubits; and its corners, and its length, and its walls, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of wood: and he said to me, This ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the table that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " before the LORD.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the temple and the sanctuary had two doors.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the doors had two leaves each, two turning leaves; two ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "leaves",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for the one door, and two leaves for the other ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "door",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " made on them, on the doors of the temple, cherubim and palm-trees, as ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " made upon the walls; and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thick planks upon the face of the porch without.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "EZK.41.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:EZK.41.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " narrow windows and palm-trees on the one side and on the other side, on the sides of the porch, and ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "upon",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the side-chambers of the house, and thick planks.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
